{"assets":[],"contestId":"53","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's go."},{"kind":"line_break"},{"kind":"line_break"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Autocomplete"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"line_break"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In this problem you should read the statement and solve in any way. One of the most simple solutions is read string and last visited pages, sort (even bubble source - 100"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"3"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" isn't a lot, 3rd power because we need 100 operations to compare two strings), and rundown pages. When we find good string, we should write it and exit."},{"kind":"line_break"},{"kind":"text","text":"If there are no such one, write source string. 'Goodness' of string is checking with one "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"if"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" (to check lengths and avoid "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"RTE"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"for"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"line_break"},{"kind":"line_break"},{"kind":"line_break"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Froggy (Little Frog)"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"line_break"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"IMHO it's the second difficulty problem. If you cannot see solution just after you saw the statement, you can write brute-force solution (rundown all permutation and check), run it for "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n=10"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and see beautiful answer."},{"kind":"line_break"},{"kind":"text","text":"Answer is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1 n 2 (n-1) 3 (n-2) 4 (n-3) ... "}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"Let's define two pointers - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"In"},{"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"the beginning, the first one will point to 1, and the second one - to n. On odd positions write down "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" (and increase it), on even - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" (and decrease it). Do it while "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l <= r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"line_break"},{"kind":"text","text":"Proof is rather easy: every jump is shorter than the previous one."},{"kind":"line_break"},{"kind":"line_break"},{"children":[{"kind":"line_break"},{"kind":"text","text":"D. Physical education"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"line_break"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This problem is also very easy. The first thing we should learn is moving element from position "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to position "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y (y < x)"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". Let's move "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x "}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"to position "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x - 1"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" with one oblivious swap. Then to position "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x -2"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". And so on."},{"kind":"line_break"},{"kind":"text","text":"Now we want to make "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"=b"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"subscript"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". Find in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" element, that equals "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a1"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and move it to the first position. Similarly we can make "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"=b"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"subscript"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". So, we have "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" steps and at every step we do "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n - 1"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" swaps at the most. "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n<=300"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", so "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n(n-1)<=89700<10"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"6"}],"kind":"superscript"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"line_break"},{"kind":"line_break"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Blog photo"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"line_break"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Due to "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/blog/entry/1059"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bug in GCC"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" I've lost 25 minutes solving this problem. In the end I've used MSVC++."},{"kind":"line_break"},{"kind":"text","text":"But it was digression, now let's think."},{"kind":"line_break"},{"kind":"text","text":"The first thing we need to do is fix one side (which are power of two). Because there are two sides and copy-paste is great place for bugs it'll be better to make one more "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"for"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" from 1 to 2 and on the 2nd step swap "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"w"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"h"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". It decreases amount of code."},{"kind":"line_break"},{"kind":"text","text":"Now we know that "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"h=2"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"superscript"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". We need to find such "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"w"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", that "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0.8 <= h/w <= 1.25. "}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"Solve inequalities for "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"w"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"h/1.25 <= w <= h/0.8. "}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"Because"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" w "}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"is integer, it can take any value from "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"ceil(h/1.25) "}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"to"},{"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"floor(h/0.8) "}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"inclusive. We need to maximize square and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"h"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is fixed, so our target is maximize "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"w"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". We need to let "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"w=floor(h/0.8)"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and check that it fit borders. If so - relax the answer."},{"kind":"line_break"},{"kind":"text","text":"It's "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O(log"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"2"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" h)"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" solution."},{"kind":"line_break"},{"kind":"text","text":"Possible bugs are:"},{"kind":"line_break"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You calculate square in 32-bit type or like this: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"int w = ..., h = ...; long long s = w * h; "}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"In this case compiler calculate "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"w * h"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"in 32-bit type first"}],"kind":"strong"},{"kind":"text","text":", and then convert it to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"long long"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". Solution is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"long long s = (long long)w * h"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"floor(0.9999999999)=0. "}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"The "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"floor"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" function does not correspond with inaccuracy of floating point types. It can be solved either with adding something "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"eps"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to number before calling "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"floor"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", or with additional check that difference between "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"floor"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"'s result and source value is not greater than "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1 - eps"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p.s. The "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"floor"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" function is up to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"8-9 times"}],"kind":"strong"},{"kind":"text","text":" slower that conversion to"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" int"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"line_break"}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"kind":"line_break"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Dead ends"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"line_break"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first thing you should notice -  - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n <= 10"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". It means, that we have exponential solution and we can rundown some subsets."},{"kind":"line_break"},{"kind":"line_break"},{"kind":"text","text":"Solution is dynamic programming "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d[m][subm]"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - number of ways to make connected tree from subgraph "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"m"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" (it's a bit mask) with dead ends "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"subm"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" (it's also a bit mask). Answer is sum of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d[2"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":"-1][x]"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", where "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"|x|=k "}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"(size of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" as a subset is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":")."},{"kind":"line_break"},{"kind":"text","text":"Recalculating isn't really hard. For empty subset and subset of two vertexes (either 0 or 1) answer is oblivious. Also you should know that there is no tree with exactly one dead end (it's easy to prove). Now for greater subsets: rundown "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" from "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"subm"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - one of dead ends. Cut it off from tree along some edge to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" shouldn't be a dead end, otherwise we got unconnected graph). Now we have tree with lower count of vertexes and either decreased 1 number of dead ends or with changed "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" (if "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" had exactly two neighbors). Answer for this tree we know already. In the end of summarizing we should divide answer by "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - each tree has been taken as many times, as it has dead ends ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":")."},{"kind":"line_break"},{"kind":"line_break"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"p.s. I'll be glad if you tell me my mistakes in English."},{"kind":"line_break"},{"kind":"line_break"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"document"},"schema":2,"sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/blog/entry/1065"}